# Updated 2026-09-09 (later same day) for a live validation pass of the
# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next ("flashnext") T1/T2/T3 patches in
# ~/Projects/vllm-qwen38next/src. BACKEND=flashnext is the ACTIVE model
# below -- the Qwen3.8-27B ("inline") forensics pass earlier today finished
# and released the GPU (confirmed via nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps
# empty before this switch); its config is commented out just below,
# unchanged, for fast switch-back. Keep header and values in agreement --
# this file is the one that bit us before (see the older NOTEs preserved
# below the commented inline block).
#
# Values MUST be double-quoted: llm and shellconfig._KV_LINE_RE only match
# KEY="value", and an unquoted line is silently skipped -- which is how this
# file previously parsed to {} and left the UI showing a stale default port.

# COLDSTART_URL is empty; Coldstart is optional and not required for this run.
COLDSTART_URL=""
# 0.95 -> 0.96 on 2026-09-09: enabling images costs 1.30 GiB of KV (0.81 GiB
# vision-tower weights + 0.49 GiB profiling/encoder), which dropped available KV
# to 6.68 GiB and made vLLM refuse to boot (262144 tokens needs 7.17 GiB). One
# extra point of util is ~0.96 GiB on this 95.59 GiB card and restores full
# context. 0.98 is known to boot then OOM under load -- do NOT exceed 0.96.
# IMAGES ENABLED 2026-09-09: --language-model-only removed (it forced every
# modality limit to 0). The companion half lives in serve.sh: images also need
# --limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":2,"video":0}, which CANNOT be expressed here --
# llm parses this file with ([A-Z_]+)="([^\"]*)" and silently SKIPS any line
# whose value contains a double quote. serve.sh therefore reads MM_LIMIT_JSON
# from the environment, defaulting to images-OFF so bin/serve-model.sh parity is
# preserved. The operator must therefore start this backend as:
#     MM_LIMIT_JSON='{"image":2,"video":0}' ./llm start
# A BARE `llm start` WILL SERVE WITH IMAGES DISABLED. Making images the default
# needs the flashnext profile in local_llm/bin/serve-model.sh to carry the same
# limit (owned by the launcher work in flight on 2026-09-09).

# --- Qwen3.8-27B ("inline") settings, kept for reference / fast switch-back -
# BACKEND="inline"
# MODEL_REPO="RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4"
# PORT="8004" (moved from 8000 on 2026-09-09): 8000 is permanently held by
# the UNRELATED ats-optimizer.service (systemd user unit, autostarts via
# default.target.wants; pid ~2922, .../ats-optimizer/.venv/bin/python -m
# src.cli serve -- confirmed with `ss -lntp`/`systemctl --user list-units`).
# That is the owner's separate work -- not stopped, disabled, or
# reconfigured. 8004 was free (`ss -lnt`) and avoids 8001 (Flash-Next),
# 8002/8003 (GLM/proxy), 8010 (coldstart), 8099 (a prior test port). Every
# other site naming the 27B's port (bin/qwen-server-run.sh default,
# servedeck.toml [backends.inline], docs/CLIENTS.md) was moved to 8004 in
# the same pass -- grep for ":8000" if one turns up unmoved.
# PORT="8004"
# EXTRA_ARGS=""
# GPU_MEM_UTIL left UNSET so the script's own hardcoded default (0.47)
# applies. 0.47 is the value the Aug 2026 crash bisection settled on after
# Xid 13/31 hit at util=.62 (Aug 23) and util=.92 (Aug 24). The 2026-09-09
# investigation re-tested util=.47, util=.62, and util=.62+--enforce-eager
# under a 7-agent growing-context load; none reproduced the fault in the
# available ~11-15 min windows (the historical incidents took 30 min to
# 30 h), so this is NOT proof .62 is safe -- it is consistent with the
# known behavior that .47 has been the actually-safe, Xid-free operating
# point for 9+ real days. Do not raise it without a multi-hour soak.
# The upstream bug (vllm-project/vllm#52225, matching RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-
# NVFP4 GDN-hybrid + MTP + fp8 KV cache on SM120 reports from other
# operators of this exact checkpoint) is still open and unmerged as of
# vLLM 0.29.0 (2026-09-09).

